DevOps Interview Command Series — Ansible (Day 12) ⚙️

Ansible is a powerful configuration management & automation tool.
From server provisioning to application deployments, Ansible enables agentless automation at scale.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Ansible commands you must know:

ansible --version

ansible all -m ping
ansible web -m ping

ansible-inventory --list
ansible-inventory --graph

ansible-playbook playbook.yml
ansible-playbook playbook.yml --check
ansible-playbook playbook.yml --diff

ansible-playbook playbook.yml --syntax-check
ansible-playbook playbook.yml --start-at-task "task-name"

ansible-playbook playbook.yml -i inventory
ansible-playbook playbook.yml -l hostgroup

ansible-doc -l
ansible-doc yum

ansible-galaxy init role_name
ansible-galaxy install role_name

🎯 Interview Focus
• Agentless architecture (SSH-based)
• Inventory & host grouping
• Playbooks, roles & idempotency
• Check mode & dry runs
• Variables, handlers & templates
• Ansible vs Terraform vs Bash
